DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((ln(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("9/((e^((x^3))))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("[0, 13] U [0, 7]");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-9, -7, -6, -2, 8}) U [0, 13] U [0, 7] U [0, 7]");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(((-infinity, 12)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 12))) U {-10, -7, 10}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(-infinity, 12) U ({-10, -7, 10} U {-2, -1, 2, 7, 8}) U {-2, -1, 2, 7, 8}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Lily started her day with [`10`] points in her classroom reward system. During the day, she completed [`11`] math challenges, but each challenge she got wrong cost her [`8`] points. At the end of the day, she didn't gain or lose any points for other reasons. What was Lily's final point total?

[_____]{-78}
[%
0+10-0-11*8

First, calculate the points lost from the math challenges: 11 × 8 = 88 points lost. Then, calculate the final points: 10 - 88 = -78 points. This means Lily owes 78 points to reach zero.
%]
---

Emma had [`13`] colored pencils. Her friend Sarah gave her [`17`] more pencils. Then Emma used [`3`] boxes of pencils for an art project, with each box containing [`11`] pencils. How many pencils does Emma have left?

[_____]{-3}
[%
13+17-3*11

First, calculate the total pencils Emma used for the art project: 3 × 11 = 33 pencils. Then, calculate the pencils she had before the project: 13 + 17 = 30 pencils. Finally, subtract the pencils used: 30 - 33 = -3 pencils. This means Emma is short 3 pencils for her project.
%]
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-2, -1, 2, 7, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x < 12\}`]
- [`C = \{-10, -7, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`((B) \cap B) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cup (C \cup A) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -7, -6, -2, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 0 \leq x \leq 13\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 0 \leq x \leq 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(A) \cup B \cup C \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 5, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -6, 2, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 7, 5, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, 2, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 5, -5>") x Compute("<-6, 2, 3>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, 2, 3>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 5, 10>") . Compute("<-6, 2, 3>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 5, 10>") x Compute("<7, 5, -5>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -1, -8, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 8, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 7, 7, 9 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 7, 9>") . Compute("<7, 8, -8>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -8, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -8, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, 7, 9>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<7, 8, -8>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
